panfrost (Valhall): honour the first instance of a draw

Panfrost only exposes start_instance/draw_parameters on Bifrost (v6-v7), and on Valhall (v9) the JM draw path never
sets the Primitive descriptor's "Instance offset", so instance-rate attributes were always fetched from instance 0.
Stock Panfrost hides this (no ARB/EXT_base_instance on v9), but Ghostty's private Mesa reports GL 4.3
(MESA_GL_VERSION_OVERRIDE, Ghostty needs it), so GTK 4's GPU renderer used glDrawArraysInstancedBaseInstance and drew
only the first item of each instanced batch: the tab bar lost all but one title, its separators and highlights.
GTK's cairo renderer avoided that but cost ~23 ms of CPU per keystroke in Ghostty (3.7 ms on the GPU renderer).

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_jm.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_jm.c
@@ -747,6 +747,15 @@
          else
             cfg.base_vertex_offset = draw->start;
 
+         /* quigon: the first instance (glDraw*BaseInstance, GL 4.2) offsets
+          * instance-rate attribute fetches; without it every draw read the
+          * attributes of instance 0 (GTK 4 GPU renderer: only the first item
+          * of each instanced batch drawn).
+          */
+#if PAN_ARCH >= 9
+         cfg.instance_offset = info->start_instance;
+#endif
+
          /* Indices are moved outside the primitive descriptor
           * on Valhall, so we don't need to set that here
           */
